  "implementation": [
    "Six user operations cover profile choices, round-scoped pages, explicit authorization, current detail, unsent cancellation and integrity-checked independent result downloads.",
    "Minimal successful idempotent receipts recheck current original-file permissions before cache access; a prior success survives later source-version change or unavailable physical storage.",
    "Browser versions require JSON text and rounds require JSON integers; no implicit scalar coercion can select a different source.",
    "One exact POST callback bypasses user-session authentication and CSRF but requires bounded raw Ed25519 receipt verification bound to the original tenant, operation, profile and target.",
    "Callback state, reserved files, evidence and audit share the worker lock order and transaction; concurrent duplicates are stable and old worker claims cannot overwrite accepted facts.",
    "Disabled exact profiles remain usable for existing receipts; removed or replaced profiles require previously stored, reverified evidence to recover the original key.",
    "Public responses omit provider accounts, tokens, targets, raw receipts, authentication references and internal content identities; current sensitive-file restrictions apply to administrators."
  ],
