  "validatedScenarios": [
    "MockMvc through the actual authentication chain, real definition publication, original upload, approval, explicit signing authorization, signed callback, separate stored result and byte-identical original.",
    "Permission revocation blocks idempotent replays; administrator cannot inspect or download sensitive originals/results; hidden pages retain a usable cursor without returning hidden file metadata.",
    "Queued callback rejected; duplicate and older revisions acknowledged without overwriting facts; conflicting revision rejected; invalid signature leaves state unchanged.",
    "Two concurrent identical callbacks commit one operation revision, one evidence entry and exactly one reservation per original; invalid proof rolls all state, files, history and audit back.",
    "OIDC exact callback requires receipt authentication; adjacent paths and ordinary writes retain CSRF. The full positive OIDC signing journey is not claimed.",
    "Callback duplicate headers, unknown-length size limit, UTF-8/media type, original key retention and storage-error classification are tested."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "No signing UI has been implemented or accepted yet.",
    "MockMvc user journeys are not browser or packaged live-HTTP acceptance.",
    "Positive signing under actual JDBC-shared OIDC sessions, packaged process crash/restart and paired backup/restore remain to be exercised as a complete journey.",
    "Browser administrator-policy and PostgreSQL image-I/O blockers remain; no bypass attempted.",
    "Actual supplier identity, embedded PDF/OFD signatures, certificate chain and trusted timestamp acceptance remain E10.",
    "No main runtime replacement, remote push, PR or CI; delivery remains behind V02."
  ],
